ifconfig wlan0 ip_addr

The above command should be a root user command

ifconfig wlan0 ip_addr  netmask 255.255.252.0

The above command is used to set the sub netmask using ifconfig command. 

ifconfig iface_name is used to display the detail's of that particular network.

HWaddr (Hardware address) (MAC address)

inet (ipaddr)

Bcast: is the broadcast address

Mask (subnet mask)


extracting `IP address` is a frequently needed task.

ifconfig wlan0 | egrep -o "inet addr;[^ ]*" | grep -o "[0-9.]*" 

